AU  - Shah, M.A.R.; Orchard, S.; Kreuzberg, E.; Braga, D.; Das, N.; Dias, A.; Kandasamy, K.; Kibria, A. SMG; Kumar, A.; Min, W.W.; Pandey, P.; Rais, M.; Sahay, S.; Saika, P.; Scozzafava, S.; Sharma, S.B.; Swamy, SL.; Kumar Thakur, T.; Vasseur, L.; Andrade, A.
TI  - Climate mitigation and biodiversity conservation: a review of progress and key issues in global carbon markets and potential impacts on ecosystems
PY  - 2024
AB  - <jats:p>Global climate mitigation policies are promoting a radical shift in emission reduction activities to achieve net-zero targets by 2050. Although recent scientific studies have  explored the impacts of some climate mitigation initiatives on biodiversity in various contexts, a global perspective of these developments is required. This report contributes to these needs and includes a current synopsis of the carbon market mechanisms implemented around the world, how these mechanisms are related to natural ecosystems, the potential impacts of their operation, and the potential contribution of natural ecosystems in the design of Nature-based Solutions to reducing carbon emissions.</jats:p>
