AU  - Barber, Jesse R.; Fristrup, Kurt M.; Brown, Casey L.; Hardy, Amanda R.; Angeloni, Lisa M.; Crooks, Kevin R.
TI  - Conserving the Wild Life Therein--Protecting Park Fauna from Anthropogenic Noise
PY  - 2009
AB  - Anthropogenic noise is a burgeoning issue for national parks. Acoustical monitoring has revealed chronic noise exposure even in remote wilderness sites. Increased noise levels significantly reduce the distance and area over which acoustic signals can be sensed by an animal receiver. A broad range of research findings indicates the potential severity of this threat to diverse taxa, and recent studies document substantial changes in behavior, breeding success, density, and community structure in response to noise. Analysis of these data make a compelling case for systematic efforts to preserve acoustic environments throughout the National Park System.
